Below is the Java source code for the Asia Pacific Airport simulation.

[REQUIRES STUDENT'S OWN EVIDENCE: A 5-minute video recording of the student running the simulation on their machine, explaining the console output and corresponding code, and packaging into TP0XXXXX CCP.zip]

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.*;

class Plane extends Thread implements Comparable<Plane> {
    int id; boolean emergency; Airport ap;
    long arrivalTime, waitTime;
    public Plane(int id, boolean em, Airport ap) {
        super("Thread-Plane-" + id);
        this.id = id; this.emergency = em; this.ap = ap;
    }
    @Override public int compareTo(Plane o) {
        return Boolean.compare(o.emergency, this.emergency);
    }
    private void log(String msg) { System.out.println(getName() + " : Plane " + id + ": " + msg); }
    @Override public void run() {
        try {
            arrivalTime = System.currentTimeMillis();
            log(emergency ? "Requesting EMERGENCY landing!" : "Requesting permission to land!");
            int gate = ap.requestLanding(this);
            waitTime = System.currentTimeMillis() - arrivalTime;
            ap.recordWait(waitTime);

            ap.runway.acquire();
            log("Landing on runway..."); Thread.sleep(500);
            log("Coasting to Gate " + gate);
            ap.runway.release();

            log("Docked at Gate " + gate + ". Concurrent servicing started.");
            Thread pax = new Thread(() -> {
                try {
                    int disembark = new Random().nextInt(50) + 1;
                    Thread.sleep(300);
                    int embark = new Random().nextInt(50) + 1;
                    ap.totalPassengers.addAndGet(embark);
                    System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " : " + disembark + " disembarked, " + embark + " boarded Plane " + id);
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {}
            }, "Thread-Pax-Plane-" + id);
            Thread clean = new Thread(() -> {
                try { Thread.sleep(400); System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + " : Cleaned & resupplied Plane " + id); }
                catch (InterruptedException e) {}
            }, "Thread-Clean-Plane-" + id);
            pax.start(); clean.start();

            ap.fuelTruck.acquire();
            log("Refuelling with exclusive truck..."); Thread.sleep(500);
            ap.fuelTruck.release();
            pax.join(); clean.join();

            log("Undocking from Gate " + gate);
            ap.runway.acquire();
            log("Coasting to runway and taking off..."); Thread.sleep(500);
            ap.runway.release();
            ap.depart(this, gate);
            log("Has departed.");
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {}
    }
}

class Airport {
    Semaphore runway = new Semaphore(1, true);
    Semaphore fuelTruck = new Semaphore(1, true);
    PriorityBlockingQueue<Plane> queue = new PriorityBlockingQueue<>();
    ConcurrentLinkedQueue<Integer> freeGates = new ConcurrentLinkedQueue<>(Arrays.asList(1, 2, 3));
    Map<Plane, Integer> assignedGate = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    AtomicInteger groundsCount = new AtomicInteger(0), planesServed = new AtomicInteger(0), totalPassengers = new AtomicInteger(0);
    List<Long> waitTimes = Collections.synchronizedList(new ArrayList<>());

    public synchronized int requestLanding(Plane p) throws InterruptedException {
        queue.put(p);
        while (groundsCount.get() >= 3 || freeGates.isEmpty() || queue.peek() != p) wait();
        queue.poll();
        groundsCount.incrementAndGet();
        int g = freeGates.poll();
        assignedGate.put(p, g);
        notifyAll();
        return g;
    }
    public synchronized void depart(Plane p, int gate) {
        freeGates.offer(gate);
        groundsCount.decrementAndGet();
        planesServed.incrementAndGet();
        notifyAll();
    }
    public void recordWait(long w) { waitTimes.add(w); }
}

public class AirportSim {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Airport ap = new Airport(); Random rand = new Random(); List<Plane> planes = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 1; i <= 6; i++) {
            Plane p = new Plane(i, (i == 6), ap);
            planes.add(p); p.start();
            Thread.sleep(rand.nextInt(2000));
        }
        for (Plane p : planes) p.join();
        System.out.println("Thread-ATC-Manager : Sanity Check - Free Gates: " + ap.freeGates.size() + "/3");
        long max = Collections.max(ap.waitTimes), min = Collections.min(ap.waitTimes);
        double avg = ap.waitTimes.stream().mapToLong(v -> v).average().orElse(0);
        System.out.printf("Thread-ATC-Manager : Planes: %d | Pax: %d | Wait(ms) Min: %d, Avg: %.1f, Max: %d%n", ap.planesServed.get(), ap.totalPassengers.get(), min, avg, max);
    }
}
```

### 1. Introduction and Assumptions Made
This report documents the design and implementation of a multi-threaded Java simulation for Asia Pacific Airport. The system models concurrent aircraft arrivals, ground operations, and departures under strict resource constraints.

**Assumptions Made:**
1. **Gate Capacity and Ground Limit:** Although the airport limit is 3 planes on the ground (including the runway) and there are 3 gates, a plane requires a guaranteed free gate before landing because there is no ground waiting area. Thus, a maximum of 3 planes can occupy the airport grounds and gates at any time.
2. **Emergency Fuel Shortage Priority:** In the congested scenario, Plane 6 arrives with a fuel emergency while earlier planes are occupying gates or waiting in the sky queue. It is assumed that an emergency plane preempts normal waiting planes in the landing queue without violating the 3-plane ground limit.
3. **Passenger Readiness:** Terminal capacity is infinite, and up to 50 passengers are immediately ready to disembark and embark as soon as the aircraft docks.
4. **Strict Thread Identity:** Every entity (Plane, Passenger group, Cleaning crew, ATC Manager) executes its own console logging on its dedicated thread to avoid one thread acting on behalf of another.

### 2. Basic Requirements Met
* **Single Runway Exclusivity:** Only one plane can use the runway to land or take off at any given time.
* **Ground Capacity Limit (Max 3 Planes):** Prevents collisions and ground deadlocks where a landed plane has no gate to coast to.
* **Sequential Flight Lifecycle:** Landing, coasting, docking, servicing, undocking, and taking off occur in strict logical order per plane.
* **End-of-Simulation Sanity Checks and Statistics:** Verifies all gates are empty and calculates min/max/average waiting times and passenger counts.

**Concurrency Concepts & Justification:**
* **Counting Semaphores (`java.util.concurrent.Semaphore`):** Used for the runway (`new Semaphore(1, true)`). The fairness parameter (`true`) ensures FIFO access to the physical runway strip once landing or takeoff clearance is initiated, preventing thread starvation.
* **Monitors (`synchronized`, `wait()`, `notifyAll()`):** Used in `requestLanding()` and `depart()` to guard the invariant that `groundsCount < 3` and a gate is available. Guarded wait loops prevent spurious wakeups and race conditions when checking queue head priority and gate availability simultaneously.
* **Atomic Variables (`AtomicInteger`) & Thread-Safe Collections:** `AtomicInteger` (`planesServed`, `totalPassengers`) allows lock-free, thread-safe increments without synchronization overhead. `Collections.synchronizedList` safely records waiting times across multiple plane threads.

**Code Snippet (Monitor & Semaphore):**
```java
public synchronized int requestLanding(Plane p) throws InterruptedException {
    queue.put(p);
    while (groundsCount.get() >= 3 || freeGates.isEmpty() || queue.peek() != p) {
        wait();
    }
    queue.poll();
    groundsCount.incrementAndGet();
    return freeGates.poll();
}
```

### 3. Additional Requirements Met
* **Concurrent Gate Operations:** Passengers disembarking/embarking and aircraft cleaning/resupplying happen in parallel across the 3 gates and within each docked plane.
* **Exclusive Refuelling Truck:** Only 1 refuelling truck exists, so refuelling is mutually exclusive across all docked planes.
* **Congested Emergency Scenario:** Plane 6 is flagged as an emergency and bypasses waiting regular planes.

**Concurrency Concepts & Justification:**
* **Fork-Join via Thread Creation (`start()` and `join()`):** When a plane docks, it spawns separate `Thread` instances for passenger handling and cleaning, while the plane thread acquires the fuel truck. Calling `pax.join()` and `clean.join()` acts as a barrier synchronization point, ensuring the plane cannot undock until all parallel servicing tasks complete.
* **Priority Queueing (`PriorityBlockingQueue`):** Implements `Comparable<Plane>` to order planes by emergency status. This provides thread-safe priority ordering so emergency aircraft move to the head of the landing queue.
* **Mutual Exclusion Lock/Semaphore (`fuelTruck`):** A binary fair `Semaphore(1, true)` models the single refuelling truck, preventing race conditions where two docked planes attempt to refuel simultaneously.

**Code Snippet (Fork-Join & Exclusive Refuelling):**
```java
pax.start(); 
clean.start();
ap.fuelTruck.acquire();
log("Refuelling with exclusive truck..."); 
Thread.sleep(500);
ap.fuelTruck.release();
pax.join(); 
clean.join();
```

### 4. Requirements Which Were NOT Met
* **Basic Requirements Not Met:** None. All basic requirements were implemented.
* **Additional Requirements Not Met:** Individual threads for each of the 50 passengers per plane were aggregated into a single passenger-handler thread per plane to keep thread creation overhead low and ensure the simulation completes well within the 60-second limit.

